.TH LOUHI-NODE 1 2026-11-20 Louhi "Louhi"
.SH NAME
louhi-node \- one node of a Louhi compute cluster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B louhi-node
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.br
.B louhi-node
.B \-\-retire
.IR NODE_ID ...
.br
.B louhi-node \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B louhi-node
is one node of Louhi: a Dannan node that advertises
.B louhi
and runs the tasks placed on it as Docker containers, restarts them by their
policy, and serves Louhi's HTTP API when a Lugh issuer and a listener are
given. It reports what it does as one JSON object per line on standard output,
a status line every
.B \-\-status-ms
milliseconds, and runs until SIGTERM or SIGINT. Stopping it leaves the tasks
running; started again, it adopts them.
.PP
Every setting is a flag, a key in the configuration file and a
.B LOUHI_*
environment variable (the key in capitals, dots as underscores:
.B api.http
is
.B \-\-api-http
and
.BR LOUHI_API_HTTP ).
The file is
.B \-\-config
.IR FILE ,
.BR $LOUHI_CONFIG ,
or
.I /etc/louhi/config.yaml
when it exists; then
.I secrets.yaml
beside it, the environment, and the flags, each overriding the one before.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " FILE"
The cluster key file, the same on every node (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-state " DIR"
The node's state directory (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-bootstrap " HOST:PORT"
A running node to join by; may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-listen ", " \-\-port ", " \-\-advertise
Dannan's listener (default 0.0.0.0:7437) and the host other nodes reach this
one at.
.TP
.BR \-\-name ", " \-\-domain
A name, and a failure domain.
.TP
.BR \-\-heartbeat-ms ", " \-\-status-ms ", " \-\-seconds
The heartbeat (5000), the status interval (10000), and seconds to run (0, until
stopped).
.TP
.BR \-\-log-level ", " \-\-log-format " text|json"
Logging.
.TP
.BI \-\-docker-socket " PATH"
Docker's socket (default /var/run/docker.sock).
.TP
.BR \-\-allow-without-user-namespaces ", " \-\-allow-unenforced-memory ", " \-\-allow-unbounded-storage
Launch tasks although the node lacks that protection; the status says so.
.TP
.BI \-\-registry " DOMAIN"
A registry images may come from; none listed allows none.
.TP
.BI \-\-registry-credential " DOMAIN=USER:PASSWORD"
A registry's credentials; keep them in
.IR secrets.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-\-api-http ", " \-\-api-https " HOST:PORT"
The API's listeners, with
.B \-\-api-tls-chain
and
.B \-\-api-tls-key
for HTTPS.
.TP
.BI \-\-lugh-issuer " URL"
A trusted Lugh issuer; may be repeated.
.B \-\-lugh-ca
names the roots its HTTPS chains to.
.TP
.BI \-\-retire " NODE_ID"
Take a node that has left for good out of this node's agreed roster, with this
node stopped, then stop.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/louhi/config.yaml
The configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/louhi/secrets.yaml
Secrets, readable by the node's user alone.
.TP
.I /var/lib/louhi
The node's state, as the packaged service has it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when it stops cleanly, 1 when it fails, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR louhi-ctl (1)
